{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have identified and fixed the issue with price rounding in the report.\n\n### Root Cause\nIn `repo/pricing.py`, `round_to_nickel(cents)` previously used integer floor division `(cents // 5) * 5`, which floored cent amounts down to the lower multiple of 5 rather than rounding to the nearest 5 cents (e.g., 23 cents was rounding down to 20 instead of rounding up to 25).\n\n### Fix\nUpdated `round_to_nickel` in `repo/pricing.py` to use `round(cents / 5) * 5` so that values round to the nearest 5 cents as expected (e.g., 22 -> 20, 23 -> 25). Added additional test cases in `tests/visible/test_pricing.py` to cover rounding up, rounding down, and exact multiples."}]},"session_id":"b824dca1-94ce-4154-be13-1ef1d48f2183"}
